WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.760
My country saved me.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.940
My country saved me and I cannot forget it.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.700
And I will fight for her as long as I draw
breath so help me God.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.680
The last great active political figure of
the 20th century

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.980
has lost his battle with cancer at age 81.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.580
John McCain, former prisoner of war and two
time presidential candidate

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.420
was a man propelled by his interpretation
of the honor code

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.360
to defy his Vietnamese captors, criticize
Republican politicians including Donald Trump,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.800
and ultimately to support some of the most
interventionist foreign policies

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.580
in modern American history.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.120
The namesake son and grandson of well known
navy admirals

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.780
McCain initially rebelled against his military
destiny,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:49.020
famously graduating 894th out of an Annapolis
class of 899.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.510
He drank and cussed, dated Florida strippers
and Brazilian heiresses

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:57.500
and crashed an alarming number of planes before
settling down to the family business of war.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.320
McCain was on the deck of the USS Forrestal

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.680
when a stray bomb ignited a fire, killing
134 servicemen

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.700
the most deadly accident in US Navy history.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.920
And then the first bomb exploded and this
knocked me about 10 feet

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:24.840
and everyone who had been near me were all
either badly maimed or killed from this explosion.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.480
Yesterday over Hanoi, three American planes
were shot down

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.180
and at least two of their pilots captured.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.860
One of them was Lieutenant Commander John
McCain, Third,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.900
the son of the US naval commander in Europe.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:45.060
I was on a flight over the city of Hanoi and
I was bombing,

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:52.440
I was hit by either a missile or anti-aircraft
fire and I ejected

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.980
and broke my leg and both arms

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.820
and went into a lake.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.170
The aviator's rebellious nature served him
well over the next five and a half years

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.929
as he inspired cellmates with loud acts of
defiance

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.940
and quiet organization of internal communication
systems

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.500
despite enduring torture that permanently
damaged his body.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.200
This experience combined with the domestic
discord he witnessed upon returning stateside in 1973

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.840
damaged his faith in American foreign policy.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.900
Silver Star, Purple Heart, Army Commendation
Medal, eight Air Medals,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.180
national defense and the rest of this garbage
it doesn't mean a thing.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.540
As a congressman McCain opposed Ronald Reagan
sending marines to Beirut.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:43.040
As a senator he criticized Bill Clinton's
nation building adventures in Somalia and Haiti

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.760
and described US military involvement in Yugoslavia
as:

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.700
The aspect of the future of this nation that
bothers me more than anything else.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.180
Yet by 1998 McCain would emerge as the Senate's
leading hawk.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.320
So what happened?

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.840
The unexpectedly easy military successes in
the Gulf War and Yugoslavia

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.700
coupled with the vacuum in post Cold War leadership

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:10.810
led McCain to re-embrace a Teddy Roosevelt
style belief in American military supremacy

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.700
and to waive off Vietnam as some sort of anomaly.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.440
"Our loss in Vietnam afflicted America witha
kind of identity crisis"

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.260
he wrote in his 1998 memoir 'Faith of my Fathers'

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:25.900
"We should never have let this one mistake,
terrible though it was, color our perceptions forever."

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.160
And I thought I would tell Senator McCain

00:03:27.169 --> 00:03:29.430
he is a man of profound personal courage

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.359
and the suffering in service he gave to this
country ought to be honored.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.260
For most of McCain's political career, he
was the media's favorite Republican.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.260
I admit I, we all rooted for you by the way

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.000
and a lot of us in this business like John
McCain a lot.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.180
The wonderful thing about McCain always has
been that he is a maverick.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:49.540
Hillary Clinton has said that you are her
favorite Republican.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:54.040
The mutual love affair with what McCain once
described as his base in the national media

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.500
soured once he won the Republican nomination.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.780
But even in 2008 the press frequently mistook
his pragmatism for a lack of ideology.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.020
In fact, it was anything but.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.620
The Arizona Senator has long had an alarmingly
martial view of citizenship.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:13.560
In which individualism must be subsumed to
the greater good.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:18.340
President Bush has talked about our staying
in Iraq for 50 years.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:21.640
Maybe a hundred, that'd be fine with me as
long as Americans-

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.200
as long as Americans are not being injured
or harmed or wounded or killed.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.340
His longest war was against what he called
corrosive cynicism.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.540
Which meant that anything creating more of
the stuff

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:36.250
from steroids in baseball, to political advertising
on Facebook was in his cross-hairs.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.040
The same sense of high moral dudgeon would
also take him to better places

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.740
such as his opposition to torture and annual
attacks on Pentagon waste.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.780
Understandably it's McCain's profound sense
of honor

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.150
that obituarists will be emphasizing in the
coming days.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.590
With his health deteriorating in 2017

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.180
the Senator led a global tour to reassure
nervous American allies,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.700
called out eruptions of conservative bigotry,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.340
and cast the deciding vote against the flawed
repeal of Obamacare.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.960
Turning the thumbs down on the repeal-

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.780
The open ended interventionism the Senator
championed in his final two decades

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:15.060
led to some of the most tragic policy failures
of our time.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:20.680
There is also honor in seeking a more humble
conception of America's role in the world.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.380
Farewell John McCain.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.280
You will make sacrifices for your fellow Americans

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.580
who won't be asked to make sacrifices for
you.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:37.040
It is a noble cause, it is your cause and
it's worth living and dying for.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:44.740
May your lives be as lucky as mine, godspeed,
semper fidelis, fair winds and following seas.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.540
Thank you.

